A||||9||ChadMan||Brakes are done!  Fiero's back!  Whooped a new Civic EX!||||10||
Z||000000||ChadMan||06-09-2000||09:14 AM||||Well, I got my new calipers on.  I want to take the car to a deserted parking lot and try a few panic stops before passing a final verdict, but they seem to be great!  No more pulling to the left and no more creaking!  Nothing like a week and a half without your Fiero to make you appreciate it.<P>On my way to work today, I got caught by a red light and had pole position.  This lowered and fart-canned Civic EX pulled up next to me in the right lane - his lane ended about 1/8 mile through the intersection.  So he kept creeping forward and blipping his throttle until he was completely forward of the crosswalk - I just sat there behind the white line and waited for the green.<P>A split-second after I saw the cross-traffic's light turn red, I gunned the Duke and popped the clutch.  The Fiero launched just as our light turned green and I spanked him good out of the hole.  He revved to what sounded like about 6000 rpm and popped his clutch, then sat there converting his front tires into clouds of white smoke.  By the time he hooked up, I had a great lead and was already shifting to second.  He was gaining fast, but nowhere near fast enough to catch me before his lane ended.  So he gave up and tucked in behind me.<P>A true kill?  Maybe not - but we Duke guys have to take what we can get!||||reg||10
Z||000001||2M4 Dale||06-09-2000||09:30 AM||||Hey...a kill is a kill. and  you got one. Lets hear it for the IRON DUKE !!!||||reg||14
Z||000002||lennyb4||06-09-2000||09:43 AM||||I love to hear about kills concerning our little iron ducks. I have two complete motor systems to switch into mine ( HO quad + 3.1 ) but the duke just runs to damn good (95,000 and purrs). ||||reg||14
Z||000003||batboy||06-09-2000||10:02 AM||||I've said this before, short races are often won at the line. Driver skill can make or break you. If this was a 1/8 mile dragstrip, you would of won regardless. It was a win.||||reg||1
Z||000004||turbo86se||06-09-2000||10:18 AM||||hey bats, wasn't that you that always had trouble with that mail jeep sneaking up on you?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I beat a 90's 5.0 Mustang with my auto 88 coupe. It was a sharp left hand turn, I had the outside lane, we both floored it, my 88 coupe hugged the turn, while that huge, heavy, ugly as he!! Mustang was all over the road! The owner was a little ticked off when he saw me laughing when he finally roared past me!!!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||Eric||06-09-2000||10:31 AM||||I had the same thing happen to me yesterday with a Lexus SC 400.  The guy driving it was in his early twenties with his hat turned around backwards so I knew he was going to bite.  I just played it real cool and when the green light came up, I dumped the clutch and got into it just enough to keep the tires from spinning.  The other dude wasn't paying attention at all and I left him two car lengths behind at 30 mph.  Unfortunatly my car ran out of steam quick and the Lexus just walked away from me.  ||||reg||1
Z||000006||loafer87gt||06-09-2000||04:57 PM||||I got SMOKED by a Grand Prix GTP the other night. He pulled up beside me and I looked over and its some guy and his wife, with his 2 kids in the back of the car. I didn't really pay much attention to him, but when the light went green, I heard him light up the tires and he was GONE! I tried to catch up, but he was doing at least 150 KPH in a 60 zone. I caught up to him at the next set of lights and kinda smiled, thinking "what a dumbass" LOL||||reg||11
